    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0159" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg41"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chevalier de Tavera to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austro-Hungarian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 30, 1889</date>.
                        (Received January 31.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. Anticipating to have to address you a
                    further communication in the name of my Government, I hasten to express you
                    herewith my sincerest thanks for the expression of your sympathy for the
                    imperial family on the occasion of the lamentable death of His Imperial and
                    Royal Highness the Archduke Rudolph.</p>
                <p>The affliction caused by this sad occurrence will be a profound one for all the
                    subjects of the Austro-Hungarian Empire, who have to bewail the loss of a Prince
                    who had already well acquired a claim to their love and gratitude by the
                    conscientious devotion with which he dedicated his brilliant and numerous
                    talents to all the duties entrusted to him by his Imperial and Royal Majesty, my
                    most gracious sovereign.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tavera.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
